  <body>
<div class="page">

<!-- 1 HERO: no top nav on the sales page. A quiet, full-width becalmed sea (Sophie, 2026-11-02: the sunset was too loud next to "Becalmed?"); the headline sits in the empty sky above the boat, the rest of the text below. Under 700px the headline moves above the image. -->
<section id="top" style="position:relative;padding:0 0 40px">
<div class="hero-wrap" style="position:relative;max-width:1920px;margin:0 auto;padding-top:3vw">
<div class="hero-sky lift" style="position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:1.6vw;text-align:center;padding:0 24px">
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A5129;font-weight:600">RECHART · The Wayfinder Method</p>
<h1 class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(56px,6.6vw,118px);line-height:.95">Becalmed?</h1>
<p class="display" style="margin:clamp(10px,1vw,18px) auto 0;max-width:30em;font-size:clamp(20px,1.85vw,32px);line-height:1.25;font-style:italic;color:#1C4F6B">Maybe you don't need a new life. Maybe you need a new direction.</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:clamp(22px,2vw,34px);line-height:1.2;color:#8A5129">Or simply another look at your compass.</p>
</div>
<img src="/images/wayfinder/hero-becalmed-sailboat.webp" alt="A small sailboat alone on a perfectly still, mirror-calm sea, soft watercolor" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:2/1;object-fit:cover;-webkit-mask-image:linear-gradient(to bottom,#000 78%,transparent 100%);mask-image:linear-gradient(to bottom,#000 78%,transparent 100%)">
</div>
<div class="lift" style="max-width:700px;margin:-6px auto 0;padding:0 24px;text-align:center">
<p class="hand" style="display:inline-block;margin:0 0 6px;padding:6px 16px;border:1.5px solid #B87345;border-radius:999px;font-size:20px;color:#8A5129;transform:rotate(-2deg)">We set sail on Sunday, 3 January 2027</p>
<p style="margin:18px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">You have a life. A job. People. Responsibilities. Maybe even a perfectly decent coffee machine. And yet, something feels… off.</p>
<p style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.6;color:#3E4852">RECHART is a self-paced training for exactly this moment: to pause, find your bearings and work out what comes next. Without burning your life down first.</p>
<!-- no buttons in the hero on purpose (Sophie, 2026-11-02): let people stop and connect first; only a quiet cue to read on -->
<a href="#recognition" aria-label="Read on" style="display:inline-flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:2px;margin-top:30px;min-width:44px;min-height:44px;text-decoration:none;color:#8A5129">
<svg width="28" height="56" viewBox="0 0 28 56" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 2 C 6 16, 22 26, 14 44" fill="none" stroke="#B87345" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-dasharray="2 6" stroke-linecap="round"></path><path d="M7 38 L14 47 L21 38" fill="none" stroke="#B87345" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
</a>
</div>
</section>

<!-- route divider -->
<div aria-hidden="true" style="max-width:1100px;margin:0 auto;height:120px;position:relative">
<svg width="100%" height="120" viewBox="0 0 1000 120" preserveAspectRatio="none"><path d="M 180 0 C 220 80, 520 20, 640 70 S 820 120, 860 120" fill="none" stroke="#B87345" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="2 9" stroke-linecap="round" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></path></svg>
</div>

<!-- 2 RECOGNITION -->
<section id="recognition" style="position:relative;max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:20px 24px 60px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:48px">
<div class="lift" style="flex:1 1 380px;min-width:0">
<img class="bleed" src="/images/wayfinder/woman-sitting-thinking-bun.webp" alt="A woman sitting cross-legged, chin on hand, looking up and away, watercolor" style="display:block;width:100%;max-width:520px;height:auto;margin:0 auto">
</div>
<div class="lift" style="flex:1 1 440px;min-width:0">
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A5129;font-weight:600">The recognition</p>
<h2 class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(36px,3.6vw,54px);line-height:1.05">Not in a storm. Just… stuck?</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">Nothing is particularly wrong. But nothing feels particularly right, either. You keep going because, well, that's what you do. You meet expectations. You handle things. You make it work. And somewhere in the middle of all that functioning, a small but persistent voice starts asking:</p>
<p class="display" style="margin:28px 0;padding-left:0;font-size:clamp(28px,2.8vw,40px);font-style:italic;color:#1C4F6B;line-height:1.2">“Is this still what I want?”</p>
<p style="margin:0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">Maybe you've outgrown a version of yourself. Maybe your priorities quietly rearranged themselves while you were busy. (Or maybe you have absolutely no idea what's going on. Also fine.) You don't need a dramatic answer to ask a different question. And you don't need a crisis to change direction.</p>
</div>
</section>

<!-- 3 REFRAME -->
<section style="position:relative;max-width:1180px;margin:0 auto;padding:60px 24px 40px;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap-reverse;align-items:center;gap:48px">
<div class="lift" style="flex:1 1 440px;min-width:0">
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A5129;font-weight:600">The reframe</p>
<h2 class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(36px,3.6vw,54px);line-height:1.05">You don't need to fix your life. You need to reconnect with it.</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">A reset isn't necessarily about starting over. It's about stepping back far enough to see what's actually going on: what matters now, what gives you energy, what you've been carrying out of habit, what you keep postponing because something else is always more urgent.</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">And then, rather than making seventeen questionable decisions in a moment of existential enthusiasm, you explore. Curiously. Honestly. At your own pace.</p>
</div>
<div class="lift" style="flex:1 1 400px;min-width:0">
<img class="bleed" src="/images/wayfinder/man-wiping-foggy-window.webp" alt="A man seen from behind wiping a foggy window clear, watercolor" style="display:block;width:100%;max-width:560px;height:auto;margin:0 auto">
</div>
</section>

<!-- 3b A NOTE FROM ME: the personal connection comes early (Sophie, 2026-11-02); the longer About stays near the end -->
<!-- a torn-out logbook page (same paper as the ship's log below), with a small taped-on photo -->
<section id="note" style="position:relative;max-width:860px;margin:0 auto;padding:60px 24px 70px">
<div class="note-paper lift" style="position:relative;background-color:#FFF8EE;background-image:linear-gradient(90deg,transparent 62px,rgba(184,115,69,.55) 62px,rgba(184,115,69,.55) 64px,transparent 64px);padding:44px 44px 40px 90px;box-shadow:0 2px 4px rgba(20,34,48,.06),0 22px 44px rgba(20,34,48,.16);border-radius:2px 6px 6px 2px;transform:rotate(-0.8deg)">
<div aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;left:22px;top:30px;bottom:30px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:space-around">
<span style="width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:#EBDCC6;box-shadow:inset 0 2px 3px rgba(20,34,48,.25)"></span>
<span style="width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:#EBDCC6;box-shadow:inset 0 2px 3px rgba(20,34,48,.25)"></span>
<span style="width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:#EBDCC6;box-shadow:inset 0 2px 3px rgba(20,34,48,.25)"></span>
</div>
<figure class="note-photo" style="float:right;position:relative;width:190px;margin:-80px -70px 14px 28px;padding:10px 10px 12px;background:#FFFDF8;box-shadow:0 10px 24px rgba(20,34,48,.2);transform:rotate(4deg);z-index:2">
<span aria-hidden="true" style="position:absolute;top:-12px;left:50%;width:96px;height:26px;margin-left:-48px;background:rgba(231,177,132,.6);transform:rotate(-3deg)"></span>
<img src="/images/wayfinder/sophie-portrait-compass.webp" alt="Sophie, a watercolor portrait: copper curls, glasses, a soft grey scarf" style="display:block;width:100%;aspect-ratio:1/1;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% 30%">
</figure>
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:24px;color:#8A5129">A note from me</p>
<h2 class="hand note-hi" style="margin:4px 0 0;font-size:clamp(40px,4vw,54px);line-height:1.1;font-weight:400;color:#142230">Hi, I'm Sophie.</h2>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">If you decide to climb into your boat as its captain, I'll be your first mate on the way. We'll dust off the old charts together and start using the sextant again. (Okay, that might be a tiny bit cheesy. I'm keeping it.) The order matters, though: you're the captain. I'm the first mate.</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">I've been sailing the sea of change myself for a long time. I know what it's like when a storm tears at your sails. I know the whirlpool, too, when almost everything pulls you down and life is just deeply uncomfortable. And sadly I also know the moment when the wind simply disappears, and you sit alone and motionless in the middle of a huge ocean, waiting for something outside you to bring the wind back.</p>
<p style="margin:16px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">I've been through all of these. And the only reason I dare to say I can help you is that I've already done it, for myself and for others.</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:26px 0 0;font-size:34px;line-height:1.1;color:#8A5129;transform:rotate(-2deg);transform-origin:left">Sophie</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:2px 0 0;font-size:19px;color:#4A5560">your first mate, if you'll have me</p>
</div>
</section>

<!-- standout line -->
<section style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:30px 24px 90px;text-align:center">
<p class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(28px,3vw,44px);line-height:1.25">This is not a five-step plan to become your best self.</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:12px 0 0;font-size:clamp(28px,2.6vw,38px);color:#8A5129">Your best self has probably had enough meetings already.</p>
</section>

<!-- 4 METHOD INTRO -->
<section id="method" style="position:relative;max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 24px 40px;text-align:center">
<img class="bleed" src="/images/wayfinder/compass-copper-route.webp" alt="" style="display:block;width:220px;height:220px;margin:0 auto">
<p style="margin:8px 0 10px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A5129;font-weight:600">The method</p>
<h2 class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(40px,4.2vw,62px);line-height:1.05">Meet your inner Wayfinder</h2>
<p style="margin:20px auto 0;max-width:640px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">I've been incredibly inspired by the way the Polynesian wayfinders sail, from Hawaiʻi all the way to Aotearoa New Zealand. It's an old, sacred body of knowledge, and one we in the West don't really understand. We tend to be wired to think that if we set off somewhere, the journey runs neatly from A to B.</p>
<p style="margin:14px auto 0;max-width:640px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">The wayfinders think about it completely differently, and the navigator sits at the very centre of it all. They use everything: the swell of the waves, the wind, the animals, the path of the sun and the stars. It's a beautiful, intricate tradition, and it depends on the navigator themself.</p>
<p style="margin:14px auto 0;max-width:640px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">The Wayfinder Method is my small tribute to them. That's exactly why in this training you'll think, play, write, draw, choose, and look at yourself from every possible direction. We're going to take our frames apart a little. (I've never believed self-knowledge has to happen with a straight face in front of a beige background.)</p>
</section>

