<!-- 9 PHILOSOPHY -->
<section style="position:relative;max-width:1400px;margin:0 auto;padding:60px 24px 40px">
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:40px">
<div style="flex:1 1 560px;min-width:0">
<img class="bleed" src="/images/wayfinder/boarding-sailboat-from-pier.webp" alt="A woman with a backpack stepping from a pier onto a sailboat, watercolor" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto">
</div>
<div style="flex:1 1 380px;min-width:0;padding-right:20px">
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A5129;font-weight:600">The philosophy</p>
<p class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(34px,3.4vw,52px);line-height:1.1">You don't need the whole map before you begin.</p>
<p class="display" style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:clamp(24px,2.2vw,30px);font-style:italic;color:#1C4F6B">You need enough awareness to choose your next step.</p>
<p style="margin:22px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">Life rarely hands us a complete set of coordinates. Sometimes we move with clarity. Sometimes we experiment. Sometimes we discover that the destination we were so set on belongs to a previous version of ourselves. That's allowed. You can change your mind. You can take the scenic route. You can pause without declaring the whole expedition a failure. And yes, you can redraw the map.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- ABOUT THE AUTHOR, near the end, centred; the watercolor portrait is on the early note, here a more photographic full-figure "first mate" with an oar (Sophie, 2026-11-02) -->
<section id="about" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto;padding:70px 24px 20px;text-align:center">
<img src="/images/wayfinder/sophie-first-mate-oar.webp" alt="Sophie standing and leaning on an old wooden oar, in a navy blazer, jeans and white sneakers, smiling" style="display:block;width:100%;max-width:360px;height:auto;margin:0 auto 26px;-webkit-mask-image:radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 80% at 50% 50%,#000 70%,transparent 100%);mask-image:radial-gradient(ellipse 80% 80% at 50% 50%,#000 70%,transparent 100%)">
<p style="margin:0 0 10px;font-size:13px;letter-spacing:.18em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#8A5129;font-weight:600">Your first mate</p>
<h2 class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:clamp(38px,4vw,58px);line-height:1.05">A little more about me</h2>
<p class="display" style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:clamp(22px,2vw,28px);font-style:italic;color:#1C4F6B">Story writer, people-teller, endlessly curious about how minds work.</p>
<p style="margin:20px auto 0;max-width:620px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">Over the years I've met all sorts of methods and ideas, and what keeps pulling me back is how we actually work. Why do we want something? Why don't we do it? Why do we change something only long after we've known we should? And why does a game that seems completely pointless sometimes produce a perfectly sensible thought?</p>
<p style="margin:14px auto 0;max-width:620px;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">That's why I love this programme. You don't have to face these questions with a grim face. You're allowed to play.</p>
<!-- what's underneath the play: exercises mapped to research areas (source: Kincsesterkep/Ujratervezes/ujratervezes_teljes_audit.md); no clinical claims, NLP named lightly as a toolbox -->
<div style="margin:44px auto 0;max-width:720px;text-align:left">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;text-align:center;font-size:26px;color:#8A5129">What's underneath the play</p>
<p style="margin:10px auto 0;max-width:620px;text-align:center;font-size:18px;line-height:1.7;color:#3E4852">The games are playful. What sits underneath them isn't random. Over ten years I kept the exercises that actually worked, and most of them turn out to line up with well-researched ideas in psychology.</p>
<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:14px;margin-top:24px">
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;background:#FFF8EE"><p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;color:#8A5129">Starting with what matters to you</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#1C4F6B">Self-concordance · Self-Determination Theory</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3E4852">Goals that grow out of your own values tend to be the ones you keep going with.</p></div>
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;background:#FFF8EE"><p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;color:#8A5129">Your roles, not just your goals</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#1C4F6B">Identity-based approaches</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3E4852">Who you want to be in your own life shapes what's worth aiming for.</p></div>
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;background:#FFF8EE"><p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;color:#8A5129">Dreaming, then looking at what's in the way</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#1C4F6B">Mental contrasting · implementation intentions</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3E4852">Picture where you want to go, name the obstacle, then make an “if this happens, I'll do that” plan.</p></div>
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;background:#FFF8EE"><p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;color:#8A5129">Asking your fear what it's protecting you from</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#1C4F6B">Psychological flexibility</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3E4852">You don't have to get rid of the fear before you're allowed to move.</p></div>
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;background:#FFF8EE"><p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;color:#8A5129">Same picture, different filter</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#1C4F6B">Cognitive reappraisal</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3E4852">Sometimes it isn't the situation that changes first, but the meaning you give it.</p></div>
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;background:#FFF8EE"><p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;color:#8A5129">The cube, the story, the downstairs neighbour</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#1C4F6B">Self-distancing · metaphor</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3E4852">A little distance makes it easier to look at yourself honestly. (And a lot less awkward.)</p></div>
<div style="grid-column:1/-1;border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:16px 18px;background:#FFF8EE"><p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:21px;line-height:1.25;color:#8A5129">Small daily missions on paper</p><p style="margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;font-weight:600;color:#1C4F6B">Self-monitoring · attention</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;color:#3E4852">You don't analyse yourself for hours. You start noticing small things, write them down, look again.</p></div>
</div>
<p style="margin:20px auto 0;max-width:620px;text-align:center;font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;color:#4A5560">And yes, a few tools come from NLP. I keep them because I love them. None of this makes RECHART therapy or a clinical programme: it's a guided self-reflection training, built on ideas that hold up.</p>
</div>
<div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center;gap:14px;margin-top:26px">
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 20px;min-width:150px"><p class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:38px;line-height:1;font-weight:600">10 years</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:14px;color:#4A5560">of running this programme</p></div>
<div style="border:1px solid #E2D5C0;border-radius:6px;padding:14px 20px;min-width:150px"><p class="display" style="margin:0;font-size:38px;line-height:1;font-weight:600">100+</p><p style="margin:6px 0 0;font-size:14px;color:#4A5560">people have taken the journey</p></div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- CLOSING LETTER -->
<section style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:70px 24px 20px">
<div style="background:#FBF1E3;box-shadow:0 18px 44px rgba(20,34,48,.14);padding:44px 48px 40px;transform:rotate(-0.8deg);border-radius:2px">
<p class="hand" style="margin:0;font-size:24px;color:#8A5129">One more thing, before you click.</p>
<p style="margin:18px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:#2E3842">I don't know who you are. We haven't really met. And even if we had, I still wouldn't know better than you what's good for you. I think that matters.</p>
<p style="margin:14px 0 0;font-size:18px;line-height:1.75;color:#2E3842">So this isn't a recipe for how to live. I bring the questions. The answers are yours, and they might surprise you. I think that's good news.</p>
<p class="hand" style="margin:26px 0 0;font-size:24px;color:#4A5560">With love,</p>
